# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Citation File Format (https://citation-file-format.github.io/).
# Machine-readable citation metadata for GitHub, Zenodo, and FAIR tooling.
# The R-level citation lives in inst/CITATION; the canonical software metadata
# crosswalk is in codemeta.json; Zenodo deposit metadata is in .zenodo.json.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'To cite the symcompR package in publications use:'
type: software
license: GPL-3.0-only
title: 'symcompR: Symbolic Computation in R'
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-11-10'
abstract: >-
  A native R computer algebra system ported from the Python library SymPy.
  Provides exact integer and rational arithmetic, automatically simplified
  symbolic expressions, assumptions, symbolic differentiation, series, limits,
  integration and integral transforms, polynomial algebra, equation,
  differential equation, recurrence and Diophantine solvers, matrices and
  matrix expressions, number theory, combinatorics, logic, sets, geometry, and
  printers for LaTeX, MathML, two dimensional text, and source code, all
  implemented in R without a Python dependency.
authors:
  - family-names: Sophie
    given-names: Adam R
    email: adamrsophie@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/adamrsophie/symcompR
url: https://adamrsophie.github.io/symcompR/
keywords:
  - computer-algebra
  - symbolic-computation
  - symbolic-mathematics
  - sympy
  - calculus
  - polynomials
  - equation-solving
  - number-theory
  - r
